t moved to v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: every region is on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-ups: (1) find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures before deploying it again; (2) look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback after us-east."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S9bZPCV1wsuEnqVapkAybT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the latest release marked healthy. The two after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 (the current one), were both marked unhealthy. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create INC-0001 timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That means the on-call should only have been paged once. The incident describes what went wrong, both rollback attempts, the current state and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks before it's deployed again.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."